<title>ITALY: BankNapoli sale decree due this week - press.</title>
<headline>BankNapoli sale decree due this week - press.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian Treasury will this week issue a decree setting out terms for the sale of 60 percent of loss-making Banco di Napoli, newspapers reported.</p>
<p>A rescue plan for the troubled southern bank, which last year racked up the biggest losses in Italian banking history, includes a large cash injection by the Treasury and its privatisation by the end of this year.</p>
<p>Italian press reports said that banks interested in taking a stake should contact the Treasury by December 2 with the sale tender due to take place before December 20.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
